### SEC-003: Missing Transaction Boundaries
**Severity**: Critical (4)  
**Status**: **FIX PROVIDED**  
**Location**: `MrWhoOidc.ApiService/Program.cs` - Multiple endpoints

#### Issue Description

Multiple database operations without explicit transaction:

csharp
// CURRENT CODE - NO TRANSACTION
RequireAdmin(app.MapPost("/admin/clients/{clientId}/scopes", async (AuthDbContext db, Guid clientId, string[] scopes) =>
{
    var existing = await db.ClientScopes.Where(cs => cs.ClientId == clientId).Select(cs => cs.ScopeName).ToListAsync();
    var toAdd = scopes.Distinct(StringComparer.Ordinal).Except(existing, StringComparer.Ordinal).ToArray();
    foreach (var s in toAdd)
    {
        if (!await db.Scopes.AnyAsync(x => x.Name == s)) return Results.BadRequest(new { error = "unknown_scope", scope = s });
        db.ClientScopes.Add(new ClientScope { ClientId = clientId, ScopeName = s });
    }
    await db.SaveChangesAsync();
    return Results.NoContent();
}));


**Impact**: Data inconsistency and race conditions under concurrent access.

#### Fix Implementation

csharp
// FIXED CODE - WITH TRANSACTION
RequireAdmin(app.MapPost("/admin/clients/{clientId}/scopes", async (AuthDbContext db, Guid clientId, string[] scopes) =>
{
    using var transaction = await db.Database.BeginTransactionAsync();
    try
    {
        var existing = await db.ClientScopes
            .Where(cs => cs.ClientId == clientId)
            .Select(cs => cs.ScopeName)
            .ToListAsync();

        var toAdd = scopes.Distinct(StringComparer.Ordinal).Except(existing, StringComparer.Ordinal).ToArray();

        // Validate all scopes first
        var validScopes = await db.Scopes
            .Where(x => toAdd.Contains(x.Name))
            .Select(x => x.Name)
            .ToListAsync();

        var invalidScopes = toAdd.Except(validScopes).ToArray();
        if (invalidScopes.Length > 0)
        {
            return Results.BadRequest(new { error = "unknown_scope", scope = invalidScopes.First() });
        }

        foreach (var s in toAdd)
        {
            db.ClientScopes.Add(new ClientScope { ClientId = clientId, ScopeName = s });
        }

        await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        await transaction.CommitAsync();
        return Results.NoContent();
    }
    catch
    {
        await transaction.RollbackAsync();
        throw;
    }
}));


**Changes**:
1. Wrapped multi-step operations in explicit transactions
2. Added try-catch for proper rollback on error
3. Validated all scopes before adding any
4. Ensured atomicity of the entire operation

